  "course": {
    "narrative": "A 41-year-old female with a complex history of bilateral hip and knee pain, osteoarthritis, lumbar spondylosis, and sacroiliitis presented to establish care for pain management. Her past history includes retroverted hips, previous diagnoses of fractured sesamoid bones (later ruled out), and a pericardial fluid-filled cyst. She is currently taking methadone, Norco, Tenormin, Skelaxin, Wellbutrin SR, and Naprosyn. Physical examination revealed soreness and tenderness at the ankles, feet, and low back above the SI joints, along with hip pain on passive motion. The plan includes agreeing with the rheumatology referral, recommending a bone density scan, thyroid and parathyroid studies, and decreasing Naprosyn usage due to previous sulfa allergies.",
